WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.082
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online English for Academic Purposes.

2
00:00:06.382 --> 00:00:10.105
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.405 --> 00:00:16.354
Unit five: Note-Taking from Lectures. Today you will take clear and short notes while listening.

4
00:00:16.654 --> 00:00:19.237
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.433
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.447
Abbreviation.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.100
Abbreviation means a shortened form of a word.

8
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:31.207
Use an abbreviation.

9
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:34.434
Your turn. Say: Abbreviation.

10
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.638
Abbreviation.

11
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:40.106
Symbol.

12
00:00:41.117 --> 00:00:43.372
Symbol means a sign that means something.

13
00:00:43.983 --> 00:00:45.948
Use a symbol for because.

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.877
Your turn. Say: Symbol.

15
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:52.583
Symbol.

16
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.165
Outline.

17
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.811
Outline means a plan with main points.

18
00:00:58.417 --> 00:00:59.696
Write an outline.

19
00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.541
Your turn. Say: Outline.

20
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:06.366
Outline.

21
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:08.257
Signpost.

22
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.923
Signpost means a phrase that shows structure.

23
00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:14.296
Listen for signposts.

24
00:01:14.883 --> 00:01:17.849
Your turn. Say: Signpost.

25
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.817
Signpost.

26
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:23.538
Highlight.

27
00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:26.805
Highlight means to mark important points.

28
00:01:27.417 --> 00:01:28.905
Highlight key terms.

29
00:01:29.517 --> 00:01:32.041
Your turn. Say: Highlight.

30
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.901
Highlight.

31
00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:37.465
Review.

32
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.159
Review means to look at again.

33
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:42.274
Review notes tonight.

34
00:01:42.883 --> 00:01:45.280
Your turn. Say: Review.

35
00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.065
Review.

36
00:01:49.817 --> 00:01:50.841
Summarise.

37
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.291
Summarise means to give the main points shortly.

38
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:56.326
Summarise the lecture.

39
00:01:56.917 --> 00:01:59.627
Your turn. Say: Summarise.

40
00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:03.665
Summarise.

41
00:02:04.417 --> 00:02:05.104
Gap.

42
00:02:06.117 --> 00:02:07.791
Gap means a missing part.

43
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:09.802
Fill the gaps later.

44
00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:12.872
Your turn. Say: Gap.

45
00:02:15.733 --> 00:02:16.491
Gap.

46
00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.811
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:21.650 --> 00:02:24.671
Visal, I cannot write everything the lecturer says.

48
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:35.822
You should not. Write only key words and numbers. Use abbreviations and symbols, such as w for with and an arrow for leads to.

49
00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:38.591
How do I follow the structure?

50
00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:50.497
Listen for signposts such as firstly, another point is and in conclusion. Put each main point on a new line and indent the details under it.

51
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:53.223
What do I do afterwards?

52
00:02:54.317 --> 00:03:02.356
Review your notes the same day, fill the gaps and write a three-sentence summary. This helps you remember the lecture.

53
00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.977
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:05.817 --> 00:03:09.442
Grammar focus: Reduced forms and abbreviations.

55
00:03:09.742 --> 00:03:11.021
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:11.717 --> 00:03:14.436
for example e.g. shows an example.

57
00:03:15.350 --> 00:03:17.512
approximately approx. means about.

58
00:03:18.467 --> 00:03:25.426
Use common abbreviations such as e.g., i.e., etc. and approx. Make sure you can read your own short forms later.

59
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:29.660
Be careful! Don't say: I write all what he says.

60
00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.959
Say: I write only key words.

61
00:03:34.259 --> 00:03:35.713
Choose key words only.

62
00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.292
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.333
After the Lecture.

64
00:03:41.633 --> 00:03:44.341
Chantha listens to a lecture on climate change.

65
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:48.831
She writes only key words and uses arrows and abbreviations.

66
00:03:49.833 --> 00:03:53.249
She listens for signposts such as firstly and in conclusion.

67
00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:56.755
That evening she fills the gaps in her notes.

68
00:03:57.767 --> 00:04:00.950
Then she writes a short summary in three sentences.

69
00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:05.987
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.000
Good notes contain mostly key blank.

71
00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:12.884
A, stories. B, songs. C, words.

72
00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:18.712
The answer is C: words.

73
00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.223
Firstly is a blank.

74
00:04:21.523 --> 00:04:25.246
A, signpost. B, gap. C, symbol.

75
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.241
The answer is A: signpost.

76
00:04:32.383 --> 00:04:34.267
e.g. means for blank.

77
00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:38.092
A, energy. B, example. C, evening.

78
00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.970
The answer is B: example.

79
00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:47.244
You should review notes the blank day.

80
00:04:47.544 --> 00:04:50.733
A, next year. B, last. C, same.

81
00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.371
The answer is C: same.

82
00:04:57.517 --> 00:05:00.735
Chantha writes a summary in blank sentences.

83
00:05:01.035 --> 00:05:04.271
A, three. B, thirty. C, none.

84
00:05:07.833 --> 00:05:09.427
The answer is A: three.

85
00:05:10.633 --> 00:05:13.820
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:14.683 --> 00:05:16.625
How do you take notes in a lecture?

87
00:05:25.417 --> 00:05:26.801
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:27.101 --> 00:05:38.336
I write only key words and numbers and use abbreviations and symbols. I listen for signposts to find the structure. After the lecture I fill the gaps and write a short summary.

89
00:05:38.636 --> 00:05:40.507
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:41.417 --> 00:05:46.391
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and reduced forms and abbreviations.

91
00:05:46.691 --> 00:05:50.969
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:05:51.269 --> 00:05:53.944
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

93
00:05:54.244 --> 00:05:57.013
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

